<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ciaruteun inscription</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">5th century</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Ciaruteun inscription is a 5th-century stone inscription found in the Ciaruteun stream near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bogor">Bogor</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-java">West Java</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indonesia">Indonesia</a>. Written in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sanskrit">Sanskrit</a> in a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pallava-script">Pallava script</a>, it is carved with a pair of footprints that it compares to those of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vishnu">Vishnu</a> and attributes to King Purnawarman of Tarumanagara. It is among the oldest written records of Indonesia.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ciaruteun-inscription.jpg" alt="Ciaruteun inscription" width="320" height="393" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Isidore van Kinsbergen · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:KITLV_87655_-_Isidore_van_Kinsbergen_-_Inscribed_stone_at_Tjiaroeteun_at_Buitenzorg_-_Before_1900.tif" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
